  blockTitle: AT422-115:Pilaster Base
  blockDescription: This base bears the scotia-torus-scotia molding with bilateral
    symmetry in the diagonal axis, and thus is identified as one of the two pilaster
    bases at the rear corners of the temple.
  blockPlacement: AT422 is a fragment that with AT115 and other unnumbered fragments,
    form a pilaster base. Found in the NE quadrant, it is restored at the left rear
    corner of the temple.
  blockDrawing1: {fileID: 0}
